00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:05.055
What do you have to say for
yourself, hypocrite? Hypocrite!

00:17:08.294 --> 00:17:11.173
Do it, Kato! Knock his block off!

00:17:11.197 --> 00:17:12.307
Yeah!

00:17:12.331 --> 00:17:18.346
Oh, come on, you guys really
are stupid. You don't know a thing.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:22.484
I'm the strongest one here out of all of us.

00:17:22.508 --> 00:17:24.619
I was telling you this out of
the goodness of my heart,

00:17:24.643 --> 00:17:29.257
and this is the way you treat me?
Isn't something wrong with that?

00:17:29.281 --> 00:17:31.359
Shall I crush your arm?

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:35.047
That way you'll know who to follow.

00:17:37.923 --> 00:17:39.701
Let go of his arm!

00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:40.702
Kei...

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:41.937
Let go of him!

00:17:41.961 --> 00:17:45.207
Think you can shoot me?
Your head will explode.

00:17:45.231 --> 00:17:46.942
Okay, then here.

00:17:46.966 --> 00:17:49.025
You'll lose an arm, too.

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:54.163
You said that we're alive.

00:17:55.641 --> 00:17:59.020
But back there, it seemed as though
normal people couldn't see us.

00:17:59.044 --> 00:18:00.889
So how can we be alive?

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:02.824
That's something that's been bothering me.

00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:06.862
Are we really alive? Are we?

00:18:06.886 --> 00:18:08.396
Yes.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.798
You're not making this up?

00:18:09.822 --> 00:18:13.969
The people who come here were
rescued moments before they died.

00:18:13.993 --> 00:18:15.537
That's probably what you believe.

00:18:15.561 --> 00:18:19.574
--Are you saying that's not true?
--Probably. The way I see it,

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:23.865
the original really is dead.

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:31.686
The people who are here
came out of a fax machine.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.889
Original? Original what?

00:18:33.913 --> 00:18:36.057
When you go home...

00:18:36.081 --> 00:18:38.627
...you shouldn't talk to anyone about this.

00:18:38.651 --> 00:18:40.415
He vanished!

00:18:48.661 --> 00:18:51.596
They wouldn't believe you anyway.

00:19:16.922 --> 00:19:18.867
Mom...

00:19:18.891 --> 00:19:20.035
Money?

00:19:20.059 --> 00:19:22.118
I still have enough for this month.

00:19:23.729 --> 00:19:27.029
No, it's nothing, really.

00:19:39.812 --> 00:19:41.957
And now, this morning's news.

00:19:41.981 --> 00:19:44.926
A forty-year-old woman gave
birth via Caesarean section,

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.062
but died of shock from the loss of blood.

00:19:47.086 --> 00:19:48.797
More on this later.

00:19:48.821 --> 00:19:50.332
This was all just a dream.

00:19:50.356 --> 00:19:53.168
--In other news, a member of Parliament...
--There's no way it could've been real.

00:19:53.192 --> 00:19:56.071
...died last night at a Tokyo hospital.

00:19:56.095 --> 00:19:56.538
"Goro Suzuki (64)"
...died last night at a Tokyo hospital.

00:19:56.562 --> 00:19:58.039
"Goro Suzuki (64)"
The deceased Goro Suzuki

00:19:58.063 --> 00:20:01.710
"Goro Suzuki (64)" was a veteran who
was elected to the lower house five times.

00:20:01.734 --> 00:20:02.277
"Goro Suzuki (64)" But he'd been hospitalized
for liver cancer since the end of last year.

00:20:02.301 --> 00:20:06.081
But he'd been hospitalized for liver
cancer since the end of last year.

00:20:06.105 --> 00:20:10.051
A date for the special election
to fill Mr. Suzuki's seat

00:20:10.075 --> 00:20:12.203
has not yet been announced.

00:20:13.612 --> 00:20:17.559
--Next, sometime last night there was a collision between a scooter...
--It had to be a dream.

00:20:17.583 --> 00:20:20.795
...and a compact car at the intersection
of the Oume Highway and Loop 8.

00:20:20.819 --> 00:20:23.531
Masashi Yamada was killed in the accident.

00:20:23.555 --> 00:20:27.458
Mr. Yamada was an elementary school teacher...

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.142
Can you believe this?

00:20:34.166 --> 00:20:37.712
Two high school boys
have mysteriously vanished.

00:20:37.736 --> 00:20:41.616
They say the two helped a homeless man
and were run over by the subway.

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:45.120
--If that is the case, why would the two disappear
--That's right, my umbrellal If it's here, then...

00:20:45.144 --> 00:20:48.490
--after performing such a noble act?
--Yes, that's it! It was just a dream.

00:20:48.514 --> 00:20:51.359
At present, the Tokyo
Metropolitan Police Department

00:20:51.383 --> 00:20:54.195
is investigating the case as both
an accident and an incident.

00:20:54.219 --> 00:20:56.164
Back to you, Mr. Morikawa.

00:20:56.188 --> 00:20:59.920
Thank you. This program...

00:21:02.561 --> 00:21:04.256
No way!

00:21:12.404 --> 00:21:14.930
So it wasn't just a dream.

00:21:22.815 --> 00:21:29.949
Hajimari wa dare demo junshin muku na baby

00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:41.457
Nigai mi kajitte mo
kujikecha dame yo walk straight

00:21:46.004 --> 00:21:54.004
Satta koto da kedo
ame no naka zukizuki itamu yo

00:22:00.119 --> 00:22:02.363
I'm lonely as floating ice

00:22:02.387 --> 00:22:07.202
Yaseta yubi ni kiss o shite

00:22:07.226 --> 00:22:13.908
Naita anata o omoidasu yo

00:22:13.932 --> 00:22:18.780
Kore de owari da to shite mo

00:22:18.804 --> 00:22:23.685
Saigo no kiss wa wasurenai yo

00:22:23.709 --> 00:22:31.709
Wasurenai yo... Wasurenai yo...

00:22:35.621 --> 00:22:38.621
Kare no kiss o wasurenai yo
